---
jpsType: update
id: wordpress-multinode-fix-php-config
name: Fix OPcache and Redis PHP config
description: |
  One-shot repair for environments provisioned before v1.2.19.

  Re-lays /etc/php.d/opcache.ini and /etc/php.d/redis.ini on the cp node
  (both wiped by a Jelastic PHP engine redeploy, which also resets
  /etc/php.ini to vanilla and strips the installer's zend_extension and
  extension lines), restarts php-fpm, and re-installs events.jps so the
  onAfterRedeployContainer hook that prevents a recurrence is registered
  going forward.

baseUrl: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shaundma/wordpress-multi-node-v2/main

onInstall:
  - restorePhpConfig
  - reinstallEvents

actions:
  restorePhpConfig:
    - log: "Restoring OPcache + Redis PHP config on cp"
    - cmd[cp]: |-
        mkdir -p /etc/php.d

        fetch_ini() {
          url="$1"; dest="$2"; label="$3"
          for attempt in 1 2 3; do
            if curl -fsSL -o "${dest}.new" "$url" && [ -s "${dest}.new" ]; then
              mv -f "${dest}.new" "$dest"
              echo "${label} deployed to ${dest}"
              return 0
            fi
            echo "Download of ${label} attempt $attempt failed. Retrying in 3s..." >&2
            sleep 3
          done
          echo "ERROR: Failed to download ${label} after retries" >&2
          rm -f "${dest}.new"
          return 1
        }

        fetch_ini ${baseUrl}/configs/php.d/opcache.ini   /etc/php.d/opcache.ini   "OPcache config"      || exit 1
        fetch_ini ${baseUrl}/configs/php.d/redis.ini     /etc/php.d/redis.ini     "Redis + igbinary"    || exit 1
        fetch_ini ${baseUrl}/configs/php.d/wordpress.ini /etc/php.d/wordpress.ini "WordPress PHP config" || true

        # Validate config before touching the service. If -t fails the real
        # problem is somewhere else; bail loudly rather than put php-fpm in
        # a crash loop.
        if ! php-fpm -t -y /etc/php-fpm.conf 2>&1; then
          echo "ERROR: php-fpm -t failed after ini restore"
          exit 1
        fi

        # php-fpm may be inactive precisely because the engine-redeploy left
        # it that way, so start it unconditionally when not running, reload
        # when it is.
        if systemctl is-active --quiet php-fpm; then
          systemctl reload php-fpm && echo "php-fpm reloaded"
        else
          systemctl start php-fpm && echo "php-fpm started"
        fi

        # Verify. Expect 3 matches: "Zend OPcache" + "redis" + "igbinary".
        LOADED=$(php -m 2>&1 | grep -iE "^(zend opcache|redis|igbinary)$" | sort -u | paste -sd, -)
        echo "Extensions loaded after restore: $LOADED"
        OK=$(php -m 2>&1 | grep -ciE "^(zend opcache|redis|igbinary)$")
        if [ "$OK" -eq 3 ]; then
          echo "OK: OPcache, Redis and igbinary all loaded"
        else
          echo "ERROR: expected 3 of (Zend OPcache, redis, igbinary) loaded, got $OK"
          php -m 2>&1 | head -40
          exit 1
        fi
      user: root

  reinstallEvents:
    - log: "Re-registering events.jps so onAfterRedeployContainer hook is active"
    - install: ${baseUrl}/scripts/events.jps?_r=${fn.random}
      skipEmail: true

success: |
  **PHP config repaired**

  - `/etc/php.d/opcache.ini`, `redis.ini` and `wordpress.ini` re-laid on the cp node
  - php-fpm reloaded (or started if it was down)
  - `onAfterRedeployContainer[nodeGroup:cp]` event hook re-registered so
    future cp redeploys will self-heal automatically
